digraph ReasoningTree {
  // paper_id=s41467-025-56075-7
  rankdir="TB";
  "CaseBulk" [label="(11,0,0) Currently there is: The structural and chemical evolution in the bulk of NMC particles should be considered when investigating degradation mechanisms upon cycling."];
  "CaseCalc" [label="(19,0,0) Currently there is: The calcination process can drive mass transport and reaction kinetics to redistribute constituting elements to become either homogeneously or heterogeneously distributed in NMC secondary particles."];
  "CaseDoping" [label="(18,0,0) Currently there is: Controlling materials microstructures without excessively using dopants has become an attractive strategy for long-term manufacturing reliability."];
  "CaseLimit" [label="(10,0,0) Currently there is: The effectiveness of these strategies depends on the capability to precisely control the synthesis conditions."];
  "CaseNiQuench" [label="(23,0,0) Currently there is: Some studies adopted a similar quenching treatment for Ni-rich positive electrode materials and found that Ni-rich positive electrodes could deliver enhanced electrochemical performance after the quenching treatment."];
  "CasePotential" [label="(25,0,0) Currently there is: If successful, such a thermal treatment can reduce the overall calcination duration and become an effective strategy to tailor battery performance."];
  "CaseQuench" [label="(21,0,0) Currently there is: Quenching can produce materials far from equilibrium."];
  "CaseStrat" [label="(7,0,0) Currently there is: Researchers have built functional layers on positive particles or prepared NMCs with an elemental concentration gradient and core-shell structure to mitigate surface instability of NMCs."];
  "CommonBulk" [label="(12,0,0) The common pattern is: Researchers have introduced heteroatoms into the NMC lattice, which may mitigate undesired bulk degradation."];
  "CommonCalc" [label="(20,0,0) The common pattern is: In a typical NMC calcination, the ramping and cooling rates are controlled at a few or tens of degrees per minute."];
  "CommonDoping" [label="(16,0,0) The common pattern is: It is non-trivial to precisely place heteroatoms in the desired site of NMC lattice and doping (especially multiple dopants) has vulnerable raw materials supply chain."];
  "CommonLimit" [label="(9,0,0) The common pattern is: The concentration gradient NMCs exhibit improved long-term cycle life through enhancing structural stability with a Mn-rich surface layer."];
  "CommonNiQuench" [label="(24,0,0) The common pattern is: It has remained largely unexplored regarding how quenching can change the mutual modulation between the surface and bulk of layered positive electrode particles and thus impact battery performance."];
  "CommonPotential" [label="(6,6,26) The common pattern is: There is a synergic effect between surface modification and bulk charge distribution, which is fundamentally important for designing next-generation battery cathode materials."];
  "CommonQuench" [label="(22,0,0) The common pattern is: Quenching from the peak of the calcination temperature to low temperature has been shown to increase the reversible capacity of lithium titanate negative electrodes."];
  "CommonStrat" [label="(8,0,0) The common pattern is: A surface coating layer such as Al₂O₃ can enhance the cycling stability of NMCs by suppressing undesired side reactions with the electrolyte and lowering interfacial charge transfer impendence."];
  "ConcNiQuench" [label="(0,0,0) induction: Given the induction-case that some studies adopted a similar quenching treatment for Ni-rich positive electrode materials and found that Ni-rich positive electrodes could deliver enhanced electrochemical performance after the quenching treatment, and the induction-common that it has remained largely unexplored regarding how quenching can change the mutual modulation between the surface and bulk of layered positive electrode particles and thus impact battery performance, therefore quenching shows promise but its effect on surface-bulk modulation is unexplored."];
  "ConcQuench" [label="(0,0,0) induction: Given the induction-case that quenching can produce materials far from equilibrium, and the induction-common that quenching from the peak of the calcination temperature to low temperature has been shown to increase the reversible capacity of lithium titanate negative electrodes, therefore quenching (fast cooling) can improve electrode performance."];
  "ConcStrat" [label="(0,0,0) induction: Given the induction-case that researchers have built functional layers on positive particles or prepared NMCs with an elemental concentration gradient and core-shell structure to mitigate surface instability of NMCs, and the induction-common that a surface coating layer such as Al₂O₃ can enhance the cycling stability of NMCs by suppressing undesired side reactions with the electrolyte and lowering interfacial charge transfer impendence, therefore functional layers, gradient and core-shell are effective strategies to mitigate surface instability."];
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) The paper proposes to investigate rapid quenching of nickel-rich LiNixMnyCozO2 cathode particles from the calcination peak temperature as a dopant-lean, coating-lean strategy to drive lithium outward, create a Ni-reduced Li-rich surface layer, suppress surface reactions, homogenize bulk charge distribution, and improve high-voltage cycling stability without relying on extra dopants or intricate coatings.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) When existing coating, gradient, and dopant strategies for nickel-rich NMC cathodes have surface, bulk, synthesis-control, or manufacturing limitations, and when calcination/quenching can alter elemental distributions, it is scientifically motivated to test a quenching-based route that couples surface modification with bulk charge distribution."];
  "R11" [label="(0,0,0) If a thermal treatment is successful, it should be evaluated as a way to tailor battery performance while accounting for the synergy between surface modification and bulk charge distribution in cathode-material design."];
  "R5" [label="(0,0,0) Concentration-gradient or related surface-structured NMC strategies can improve long-term cycle life through enhanced structural stability, but their effectiveness depends on precise control of synthesis conditions."];
  "R6" [label="(0,0,0) Bulk structural and chemical evolution in NMC particles is an important degradation-design consideration, as reflected both by the need to consider bulk evolution during cycling and by attempts to mitigate bulk degradation through heteroatom introduction into the NMC lattice."];
  "R7" [label="(0,0,0) Because precise heteroatom placement in the NMC lattice is non-trivial and multiple-dopant approaches can face raw-material supply-chain vulnerabilities, controlling microstructures without excessive dopant use is a motivated route for manufacturing reliability."];
  "R8" [label="(0,0,0) Since calcination can redistribute constituting elements in NMC secondary particles and typical NMC calcination controls ramping and cooling rates, calcination cooling-rate control is a plausible variable for tailoring elemental distribution in cathode particles."];
  "CaseStrat" -> "ConcStrat" [label="induction-case"];
  "CommonStrat" -> "ConcStrat" [label="induction-common"];
  "CaseQuench" -> "ConcQuench" [label="induction-case"];
